.TH WELLPER 1 "August 2026" "wellper 1.0" "wellutils"
.SH NAME
wellper \- peripheral device report (USB, displays, audio)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wellper
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wellper
inspects the system and prints a colour-coded report of attached peripherals:
USB devices (grouped by bus and classified by type), display outputs, and audio
devices.
.PP
Output is auto-scaled: when stdout is a terminal, sections are drawn as adaptive
boxes that always fit the terminal width; when stdout is a pipe or file, a plain
text layout is used. Emoji icons are enabled by default and disabled on
non-UTF-8 locales.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-lang " ru|en|auto"
Force report language. The default is \fBauto\fR, which reads the persistent
setting from \fI~/.config/wellutils/lang.conf\fR and falls back to the current
locale (Russian when the locale is Russian, otherwise English).
.TP
.BI \-\-color " always|never|auto"
Force, disable, or auto-detect ANSI colour. In \fBauto\fR mode colour is used
only on a terminal, and is disabled by the
.B NO_COLOR
environment variable or a \fBdumb\fR TERM. \fBalways\fR overrides all detection.
.TP
.B \-\-plain
Force plain text output without box drawing, even on a terminal.
.TP
.B \-\-box
Force box drawing even when stdout is not a terminal.
.TP
.B \-\-no-emoji
Disable emoji icons.
.TP
.BI \-\-groups " LIST"
Show only USB devices belonging to the comma-separated group list. Valid groups:
.BR in " (keyboards, mice, tablets, gamepads), "
.BR media " (cameras, audio, network), "
.BR other " (storage, printers, phones, hubs, misc), "
.BR all .
.TP
.BI \-\-sections " LIST"
Show only the comma-separated report sections. Valid sections:
.BR usb ", " displays ", " audio .
.TP
.B \-\-strict
Exit with status 1 when nothing is detected.
.TP
.B \-\-terse
Print one summary line (counts of USB, displays, audio) and nothing else.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit a machine-readable JSON document (validated against
.IR \-\-sections /\-\-groups ).
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Enable verbose tracing (\fBset \-x\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-
End of options.
.SH GROUPS
USB devices are classified into groups:
.TP
.B in
Input devices: keyboards, mice, tablets, gamepads.
.TP
.B media
Cameras/video, audio interfaces, and network adapters.
.TP
.B other
Storage, printers, phones, hubs, and other peripherals.
.SH SECTIONS
.TP
.B usb
USB device listing grouped by bus.
.TP
.B displays
Connected display outputs.
.TP
.B audio
Audio devices.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Nothing detected and \fB\-\-strict\fR given.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command-line usage.
.TP
.B 3
Unexpected runtime error.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B WELLUTILS_LANG
\fBru\fR or \fBen\fR; overrides locale detection.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When set (any value), colour is disabled in auto mode.
.TP
.B COLUMNS
Terminal width used for box scaling (default 100).
.TP
.B LANG / LC_MESSAGES
Locale used to pick the default language.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/wellutils/lang.sh
Translation table (read-only).
.TP
.I /usr/share/wellutils/box.sh
Adaptive box-drawing engine.
.TP
.I ~/.config/wellutils/lang.conf
Persistent language setting (default \fBRU\fR); written by
.BR wellutils (1).
.SH AUTHOR
wellbou_
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wellutils (1),
.BR wellusb (1),
.BR wellpci (1),
.BR wellblock (1),
.BR wellmem (1),
.BR wellhw (1),
.BR wellsensors (1),
.BR wellmod (1)
